# 7. Docker Networking

## 7.1 List Networks

```bash
docker network ls
```

## 7.2 Inspect a Network

```bash
docker network inspect bridge
```

## 7.3 Create a Network

```bash
docker network create lab-network
```

## 7.4 Run Containers on a Network

```bash
docker run -dit --name lab1 --network lab-network debian:bookworm bash
docker run -dit --name lab2 --network lab-network debian:bookworm bash
```

Install ping in the containers if needed:

```bash
docker exec lab1 apt-get update
docker exec lab1 apt-get install -y iputils-ping
```

Test connectivity:

```bash
docker exec lab1 ping -c 3 lab2
```

On a user-defined bridge network, containers can normally resolve each other by container name.

## 7.5 Connect and Disconnect Containers

```bash
docker network connect lab-network debian-lab
docker network disconnect lab-network debian-lab
```

## 7.6 Remove a Network

```bash
docker network rm lab-network
```

The network must not have connected containers.

