# 8. Docker Resource Management

## 8.1 Check Disk Usage

```bash
docker system df
docker system df -v
```

Displays Docker disk usage, including images, containers, and volumes.

## 8.2 Remove Stopped Containers

```bash
docker container prune
```

## 8.3 Remove Unused Images

```bash
docker image prune
docker image prune -a
```

* `docker image prune` — Removes dangling images.
* `docker image prune -a` — Removes images not referenced by any container.

## 8.4 Remove Unused Networks

```bash
docker network prune
```

## 8.5 Remove Unused Build Cache

```bash
docker builder prune
```

## 8.6 General Cleanup

```bash
docker system prune
```

Removes unused containers, networks, dangling images, and build cache.

More aggressive cleanup:

```bash
docker system prune -a
```

Include unused volumes:

```bash
docker system prune --volumes
```

**Warning:** Cleanup commands can remove resources you intended to keep. Review what will be deleted before confirming.

