# 9. Restart Policies

Restart policies control whether Docker attempts to restart a container.

## 9.1 Common Policies

```bash
docker run -d --restart no nginx:alpine
docker run -d --restart on-failure nginx:alpine
docker run -d --restart unless-stopped nginx:alpine
docker run -d --restart always nginx:alpine
```

* `no` — Do not automatically restart.
* `on-failure` — Restart after a non-zero exit, subject to the configured retry limit.
* `unless-stopped` — Restart unless explicitly stopped.
* `always` — Restart automatically, including after Docker restarts, subject to manual-stop behavior.

## 9.2 Change a Container's Restart Policy

```bash
docker update --restart unless-stopped web-server
```

Check the configured policy:

```bash
docker inspect --format='{{.HostConfig.RestartPolicy.Name}}' web-server
```

