# 10. Environment Variables and Resource Limits

## 10.1 Set Environment Variables

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app \
  -e APP_ENV=development \
  nginx:alpine
```

Inspect the container's environment:

```bash
docker exec app printenv APP_ENV
```

Avoid putting passwords, tokens, or other secrets directly in command-line arguments or source-controlled configuration files.

## 10.2 Limit Memory and CPU

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name limited-app \
  --memory=512m \
  --cpus=1.0 \
  nginx:alpine
```

Limits the container to a memory limit of 512 MiB and a CPU quota equivalent to one CPU.

Check live resource usage:

```bash
docker stats limited-app
```

