# 11. Docker Compose

Docker Compose manages applications made up of one or more services.

## 11.1 Check Compose

```bash
docker compose version
```

## 11.2 Example Compose File

Create a file named `compose.yaml`:

```yaml
services:
  web:
    image: nginx:alpine
    container_name: compose-web
    ports:
      - "127.0.0.1:8080:80"
    restart: unless-stopped
```

## 11.3 Start Services

Run from the directory containing `compose.yaml`:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

## 11.4 List Services

```bash
docker compose ps
```

## 11.5 View Logs

```bash
docker compose logs
docker compose logs -f
docker compose logs --tail 100
```

## 11.6 Stop Services

```bash
docker compose stop
```

## 11.7 Stop and Remove Services

```bash
docker compose down
```

Remove containers and networks created for the Compose project.

Remove associated named volumes as well:

```bash
docker compose down -v
```

**Warning:** `-v` can delete persistent application data.

## 11.8 Validate Compose Configuration

```bash
docker compose config
```

Renders and validates the Compose configuration.

